@startuml
' Rendered by scripts/build-diagrams.sh. Edit this file, never the SVG beside it.
' The colours, the fonts and the transparent ground come from palette.iuml.
!include palette.iuml

' What earns this picture is not the order of the states, which one sentence
' holds. It is the edge that runs backwards: a lot's lessons reach the next lot
' through a document rather than through somebody's memory, and that loop is the
' thing prose spells out worst.
'
' The labels are deliberately nouns and short verbs. A state carrying a sentence
' would have to be re-rendered every time that sentence is edited in the page
' beside it, and the page is where the sentences belong.
set separator none
hide empty description

state "Coarse intention" as Intention #line:888888;text:888888
state "Sketch" as Sketch #line:AC8148;text:AC8148
state "Specification" as Spec #line:5A9662;text:5A9662
state "Merged" as Merged #line:478ECA;text:478ECA
state "card-management.md" as Doc #line:8B8E22;text:8B8E22

Intention --> Sketch : filed
Sketch --> Spec : **the lot opens**\nthe card is rewritten
Spec --> Merged : one card,\none pull request
Merged --> Doc : what the lot taught
Doc --> Spec : shapes the next\nrewrite

note right of Sketch
  Backlog. Reading one as
  settled is the mistake
  this page prevents.
end note

note right of Spec
  Todo. Written against the
  tree as it stands now.
end note
@enduml
